    "title": "Portland Trail Blazers Have Been Sold - NewsBreak",
    "text": "The 2025 NBA offseason has been extraordinary for fans. Major ownership changes are sending shockwaves through the league. Recently, the NBA approved the sale of the Boston Celtics for $6.1 billion. Now, attention has turned to the Portland Trail Blazers. ESPN insider Shams Charania broke the news that the team has reached a massive sale agreement. Tom Dundon, the current owner of the NHL’s Carolina Hurricanes, has agreed to purchase the Trail Blazers from the estate of Paul G. Allen. The deal reportedly values the franchise at over $4 billion. “ NHL Carolina Hurricanes owner Tom Dundon has agreed to buy the Portland Trail Blazers from the estate of Paul G. Allen for a valuation of over $4 billion, sources tell ESPN ,” Charania reported. Allen first acquired the Trail Blazers in 1988 for just $70 million. He remained the team’s owner until his passing in 2018 due to complications from non-Hodgkin lymphoma. Since then, his sister, Jody Allen, has overseen the franchise as chair. Alongside the NBA team, Allen also owned the NFL’s Seattle Seahawks and a 25 percent stake in MLS’ Seattle Sounders. However, neither of these assets is included in the current deal. ESPN explained the reasoning behind the trust’s decision to sell the team. They pointed to several major developments over the past year. “The trust made the decision to sell the Blazers in the wake of several key developments over the past year. The NBA agreed to new 11-year media rights deals with ESPN, NBC, and Amazon for a combined $77 billion. In 2024, the Blazers sold their home arena, the Moda Center, to the City of Portland for $1 and the land under the arena for $7 million. It then launched a public-private partnership to renovate the arena and the surrounding area that included a new lease through 2030 ,” the report read . On the basketball side, the Blazers closed last season with a 36-46 record. It remains to be seen if the new authority can steer the franchise toward better results. The post Portland Trail Blazers Have Been Sold originally published on Total Pro Sports .",
